---
title: Duck rice
servings: 4
tags: [duck, weekend]
source: Duck Rice by StarChefs, https://www.starchefs.com/recipes/duck-rice
---

> A restaurant batch: the stocks, cure, paste and pickle make far more than four plates need.

== Roasted vegetable stock ==

Put the @onions{360%g}(diced), @celery{360%g}(diced), @carrots{160%g}(diced), @red bell peppers{200%g}(diced), @vegetable bouillon{120%g}, @button mushrooms{84%g}, @leeks{80%g}(diced), @garlic{25%g}(diced), @salt{24%g}, @guajillo chiles{15%g}, @ground black pepper{6%g}, @coriander seeds{6%g}, @chiles de arbol{2%g}, @thyme{2%g}, @rosemary{2%g}, @bay leaf{1%g} and @saffron{0.5%g} in a #stockpot{} with @water{4.8%kg}.

Bring to the boil over medium-high heat, then simmer until it tastes rich enough. Strain and refrigerate.

== Oxtail stock ==

Brown the @oxtail{3.6%kg}(cut up) well in a #rondeau{} over medium-high heat. Add the @white wine{150%g} and let it reduce a little.

Pour in 4.5 kg of the vegetable stock and simmer until the meat is tender. Strain, keeping the stock and the oxtail apart.

Whisk the @white miso{26%g} into the hot stock and refrigerate both.

== Paprika cure ==

Mix the @fine salt{240%g}, @granulated sugar{120%g}, @sweet paprika{12%g}, @garlic powder{12%g}, @smoked paprika{6%g}, @ground cinnamon{10%g} and @ground sumac{40%g}.

== Cured duck ==

Lay the @duck breasts{}(magret) in a shallow #hotel pan{} and coat them evenly with the cure. Cover and refrigerate overnight.

== Rice paste ==

Heat the @olive oil{60%g} in a #saucepan{} over medium heat. Soften the @carrots{148%g}(diced), @squash{140%g}(diced), @onions{68%g}(diced) and @garlic{6%g}(diced) in it.

Add the @Campari tomatoes{14%g}, @thyme{3%g}, @sweet paprika{1%g}, @saffron{0.08%g} and 3 g of the paprika cure, and cook until fragrant.

Add the @chicken glaze{200%g} and @orange juice{20%g} and cook until thick. Blend smooth in a #blender{} and refrigerate.

== Pickled cauliflower ==

Put the @cauliflower{}(in florets) in a non-reactive container.

Bring the @distilled vinegar{600%g}, @granulated sugar{200%g}, @kosher salt{32%g}, @garlic{32%g}(sliced), @coriander seeds{7%g}, @cinnamon sticks{5%g}, @chiles de arbol{4%g}, @bay leaf{2%g}, @ground cardamom{2%g} and @water{500%g} to the boil in a #saucepan{}. Pour over the cauliflower, cool, cover and refrigerate.

== Carrot purée ==

Cover the @carrots{200%g}(sliced), @bouquet garni{5%g} and @kosher salt{2%g} with water in a #saucepan{} and cook over medium-high heat until the carrots are tender.

Drain, then blend with the @butter{40%g} until smooth and glossy. Refrigerate.

== Rice ==

Warm 360 g of the oxtail stock in a #saucepan{}.

Heat the @olive oil{80%g} and @white sofrito{150%g} in a #paella pan{} over medium heat until fragrant. Stir in 280 g of the rice paste and cook ~{2%minutes}.

Add the @short-grain rice{240%g} and toast it evenly. Add the @fermented tomato water{140%g} and @orange juice{40%g}, then the warm stock and the @cremini mushrooms{40%g}(diced).

Bring to a simmer, then lower the heat and cook until the rice is about 90 percent done. Spread it out flat and let it cool.

== Assembly ==

Warm 120 g of the oxtail stock, and separately as much carrot purée as you need.

Rinse the cure off the duck and pat it dry.

In a 14-inch #paella pan{} over high heat, cook 285 g of the rice with the warm stock and some of the pulled oxtail until the rice is tender and glossy.

Sear the duck skin side down in a #sauté pan{} over medium heat until the fat has rendered and the skin is crisp. Rest, then slice.

Plate the rice and top with the duck, carrot purée and some pickled cauliflower. Finish with @olive oil{} and @citrus zest{}.
